{"descriptionModels":[{"description":"Conditional Feat: This feat doesn\u0027t grant an Ability Score Improvement, regardless if you received it at 1st level or higher, but it doesn\u0027t count as a Feat for the purposes of training and can be taken freely at 1st level at your GM\u0027s discretion without counting as an Origin feat.\n\nYou are an adolescent, someone who has absolutely no place in the dangerous adventuring life. Perhaps you are destined to change the world and your destiny will not wait for maturity, or perhaps you have thrown your lot in with an adventuring party who has promised to keep you safe from harm. Somehow, you are at the precipice of adventure, and have the following traits:\n\n- You are considered one size smaller than normal for the purposes of ability checks, movement through tight spaces, carrying weight and the weight you can push, drag, or lift.\n\n- You have two fewer skill proficiencies than other characters of the same class.\n\n- Your Strength and Constitution scores have a maximum of 16, instead of 20.\n\n- You gain proficiency in one saving throw of your choice.\n\nWhen you reach adulthood or a state that can be considered as one, the reduced Strength and Constitution caps is removed and you can choose to exchange your extra saving throw proficiency per two skill proficiencies. Then, you remove this feat.","level":1}],"id":"Customa553c8d7-5ffe-464b-9144-97ca13c760a7","isFeature":false,"jsonType":"feat","level":1,"name":"Child [VSS] [SM] [CF]","notes":"","type":"Feat"}